t(Q-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 7 \\\\ 7 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-7\\cdot 7 & =0 \\\\ 4-2\\lambda -2\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-49 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda -45 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{4\\pm \\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+4\\cdot 1\\cdot 45}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm \\sqrt{196}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm 14}{2} \\\\  & =-5,9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =-5$ and $\\lambda =9.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357550 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186357322 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357550 #edb/ref 1069 "q-9348" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357550 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357550 #edb/ref 1071 "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$L=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357550 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b9a0d751-b8e6-598d-8c36-71f74a16fdfb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357550 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by writing the matrix $L-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nL-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 5 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(L-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(L-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 5 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(-1-\\lambda )-5\\cdot 2 & =0 \\\\ -2+\\lambda -2\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-10 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -12 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{1\\pm \\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+4\\cdot 1\\cdot 12}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\pm \\sqrt{49}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\pm 7}{2} \\\\  & =-3,4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =-3$ and $\\lambda =4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402509 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402510 #edb/ref 17592186045